        "original_id": "60d5cfad-ae75-5d97-bc24-393236a77f5e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Juniper, Indigofera\n- Taxonomy: Juniperus, Cupressaceae, Fabaceae\n- Places: James Wild Horse Trap\n- Structures: corral, fences\n\nFacts:\n- Juniper is a coniferous plant in the genus Juniperus of the cypress family Cupressaceae.\n- Indigofera is a large genus of more than 750 species of flowering plants in the family Fabaceae.\n- James Wild Horse Trap was the location of a corral and fences used to capture wild horses.\n- The corral and fences at James Wild Horse Trap were built from dead Juniper trees.",
